# Paca (Lotophagoi board)

Local UI: http://localhost:8090 — project **Lotophagoi**.

Every agent and sub-agent **must** have a nick + title. Every Paca comment, status note, and report line starts with:

`[@nick · Title]`

Task titles use this template (pipe is `│`, U+2502):

`Ortam │ State │ Title`

- **Ortam** — where in the product (`Hub`, `Lotus`, `Kiklop`, `Tooling`, `Art`, `Process`, `Production`, `Research`). Not a file path.
- **State** — which game/system component (`Island stops`, `Hallucination`, `Core loop`, `Map background`, `Paca roster`…). Not the kanban column.
- **Title** — the work itself. Never put `Backlog` / `In Progress` / `Done` in the title; that lives only in the Paca status column.

Example: `Hub │ Island stops │ Hover-grow + info tag`

Comments are readable prose, not telegrams: complete sentences, short paragraphs, file/commit names in backticks. Signature on the first line, then a blank line, then the body.

Never post anonymously. Never borrow a parent agent's nick. Report into `@nile` (game producer) → `@atlas` (board) / `@mira` (scope) / `@rex` (tech).

## Sprint + kart disiplini

Substantive work (new feature, visual slice, research tour, tooling gate) starts only after a Paca card exists with an `Ortam │ State │ Title` name. That card sits on the **current open sprint**. If there is no open sprint, `@nile` creates one before anyone writes code — sprint-less cards are board clutter, not a plan.

Kanban status lives only in the Paca column (`Todo` / `In Progress` / `Done`), never in the title. In Progress also means a matching claim line in `docs/production/ACTIVE_WORK.md`.

When sahip commits the work, move the card to Done and leave a signed comment that cites the commit hash in backticks. Research and tooling artifacts get cards too (same as playable slices).

Do not start a second expensive visual slice on the same screen or asset family while another card in that area is In Progress — `docs/production/visual-change-gate.md` + `ACTIVE_WORK.md`.

